# Styles

Choose a style by its role, such as primary text, canvas, focus or error. Then take the value from the page that owns it. The same semantic tokens apply to native Home Assistant controls, maintained custom cards and documentation examples.

## Choose a style

- [Colour roles and accessibility](brand-colour.html): choose a colour by its job and test the combination.
- [Colour](colour.html): how civica uses the GOV.UK palette, and the seven theme colours a household can choose.
- [Web](colour-web.html), [App](colour-app.html) and [Print](colour-print.html) colours: every GOV.UK value, ready to copy.
- [Data visualisation](brand-data.html): choose and compose charts, dashboards and maps.
- [Chart colour](chart-colour.html): give each chart series a stable colour, backed by patterns and labels.
- [Typography](typography.html): set sizes that keep labels, values and headings readable.
- [Typography in context](brand-typography.html): decide how type behaves in values, native screens and printed handovers.
- [Layout and spacing](layout.html): keep the hierarchy at every width.
- [Icons and images](images.html): give every meaningful icon or image a text alternative.

